<div class="prose" style="margin-top: 3rem;">
  <h2>Essential Beginner Guide: 3 Concepts You Must Not Confuse</h2>
  <p>When converting credit card points into airline miles, beginners often mix up transfer ratios with monetary valuations. Make sure to distinguish these three separate concepts:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>1. Base Transfer Ratio</strong>: How many <strong>bank points convert into how many airline miles</strong> (a quantity-to-quantity exchange). For example, Chase UR (US) to United is <code>1,000 : 1,000</code> (1:1); US Amex MR to Cathay Pacific Asia Miles is <code>1,000 : 800</code> (5:4); certain regional bank campaigns may use <code>15 : 1</code>. This is what you enter in the ratio fields above.</li>
    <li><strong>2. Transfer Bonus</strong>: An <strong>extra percentage of miles</strong> awarded during a limited-time bank promotion (e.g., a +20% bonus). Enter <code>0%</code> when no promotion is active.</li>
    <li><strong>3. Monetary Valuation (Cents Per Point / Mile)</strong>: How much <strong>cash value 1 point or 1 mile is worth</strong> (e.g., <code>1.5¢/mile</code>). <strong>Never enter a cent-per-mile valuation like 1.5¢ into the Base Transfer Ratio field!</strong> To estimate the dollar value of a miles balance, use our <a href="/en/calculators/points-to-dollars/">Miles to Dollars Calculator</a>; to evaluate a specific flight redemption against its cash ticket price, use our <a href="/en/calculators/cents-per-point/">Cents Per Point (CPP) Calculator</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How to Convert Points to Airline Miles</h2>
  <p>The math behind converting your flexible credit card rewards (like Chase Ultimate Rewards or Amex Membership Rewards) into airline miles relies on four standard rules:</p>
  
  <div class="math-formula">
    <strong>Standard Conversion Formula:</strong><br><br>
    <em>Transferable Points = floor(Bank Points / Increment) × Increment</em><br>
    <em>Threshold Requirement: Total Transferable Points must be an integer multiple of the Increment AND ≥ Minimum Transfer Threshold (minimum valid transfer = ceil(Minimum Transfer Threshold / Increment) × Increment)</em><br>
    <em>Base Miles = Transferable Points × (Airline Miles Y / Bank Points X)</em><br>
    <em>Bonus Miles = Base Miles × Bonus Percentage</em><br>
    <em>Total Miles = Base Miles + Bonus Miles</em>
  </div>

  <h3>Calculation Examples</h3>
  
  <h4>Example 1: Standard 1:1 Transfer with a 20% Bonus</h4>
  <p>You have 50,000 Amex points and want to transfer them to Air Canada Aeroplan or Flying Blue (1:1) during a 20% transfer bonus. The minimum transfer and increment are 1,000.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Transferable Points: 50,000</li>
    <li>Base Miles (1:1): 50,000</li>
    <li>Bonus Miles (20%): 10,000</li>
    <li><strong>Total Miles: 60,000</strong></li>
  </ul>

  <h4>Example 2: Non-1:1 Transfer with Step Restrictions</h4>
  <p>Suppose you have 50,500 <a href="/en/values/capital-one-miles/">Capital One Miles</a> and the selected partner uses a 4:3 transfer ratio (every 4 points convert to 3 miles, or 0.75 airline miles per bank point). With a 1,000-point transfer increment and no bonus, 50,000 points can be transferred for 37,500 miles, leaving 500 points in the account.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Transferable Points: 50,000 (500 points left behind)</li>
    <li>Base Miles (4:3 / 0.75 ratio): 37,500</li>
    <li>Bonus Miles (0%): 0</li>
    <li><strong>Total Miles: 37,500</strong></li>
  </ul>

  <h4>Example 3: Multi-Point Regional Bank Ratio (e.g., 15:1 Campaign Ratio)</h4>
  <p>Suppose your regional credit card campaign offers 1 airline mile for every 15 bank points, and you hold 15,000 points with a 1,000-point increment and 0% bonus:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Enter in the intuitive ratio fields: Every <code>15</code> bank points convert to <code>1</code> airline miles</li>
    <li>Transferable Points: 15,000</li>
    <li><strong>Total Miles: 1,000</strong></li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Points to Miles Converter vs. Transfer Bonus Calculator</h2>
  <p>Our website offers two dedicated tools for bank transfers, designed for opposite scenarios:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Points to Miles Converter (This Tool)</strong>: You know how many bank points you have, and you want to calculate exactly how many airline miles you will get.</li>
    <li><strong><a href="/en/calculators/transfer-bonus/">Transfer Bonus Calculator</a></strong>: You know the exact flight cost (e.g., you need 65,000 miles), and you want to calculate the minimum number of bank points you need to transfer to reach that target.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Where to Find Real Transfer Ratios</h2>
  <p>Never assume all transfers are 1:1. Transfer ratios, minimum thresholds, and caps vary by issuing country (e.g., US Amex vs. HK Amex), card tier, and active promotional campaigns. <strong>Always verify the live transfer rules displayed in your rewards portal before transferring.</strong></p>

  <h2>Important Transfer Rules and Limitations</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Transfers are Final</strong>: Transfers are generally one-way and cannot be reversed. Never transfer points speculatively before confirming award seat availability.</li>
    <li><strong>Minimum Transfer Threshold vs. Transfer Increment</strong>: Under this calculator's model, the total transferred amount must be an integer multiple of the transfer increment and cannot be less than the minimum transfer threshold (for example, if the minimum transfer is 1,500 and the increment is 1,000, the smallest valid transfer is 2,000 points). Check both rules in your portal.</li>
    <li><strong>Transfer Posting Times Vary</strong>: Posting times vary by bank, airline partner, and account verification status—while many transfers are instant, some partners (such as ANA or Singapore Airlines KrisFlyer) can take several hours to several business days to process according to official program terms.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Frequently Asked Questions</h3>
  <div class="faq">
    <details>
      <summary>Do all credit card points transfer at a 1:1 ratio?</summary>
      <div>
        <p>No. While 1:1 is common for US travel cards, exceptions include 5:4 (US Amex to Cathay Pacific), 4:3 (Capital One to EVA Air), 3:1 (Marriott Bonvoy to most airlines), and 15:1 or 20:1 on certain regional credit card programs.</p>
      </div>
    </details>
    
    <details>
      <summary>What is the difference between Minimum Transfer Threshold and Transfer Increment?</summary>
      <div>
        <p>The <strong>Minimum Transfer Threshold</strong> is the smallest amount required to initiate a transfer (typically 1,000 points). The <strong>Transfer Increment</strong> is the unit multiple required for the total transfer amount (total transferred points must be an integer multiple of the increment and at least the minimum transfer threshold—e.g., 1,000, 1,100, 1,200 when min transfer is 1,000 and increment is 100).</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>Why didn't my miles or bonus miles show up immediately?</summary>
      <div>
        <p>Posting speed depends on the issuing bank, partner airline system, and account status. While many partners post instantly, some airlines or batch-processed promotional bonuses can take several hours to several business days to appear per official program disclosures.</p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>
</div>

<script>
  const PRESETS = {{ transferPresets | dump | safe }};
  const $ = id => document.getElementById(id);

  let exactRatio = 1;
  let isApplyingPreset = false;
  let minTransferManuallyEdited = false;

  function findPreset(id) {
    return PRESETS.find(p => p.id === id) || null;
  }

  function updatePresetMetaUI(presetId, overriddenByUrl = false) {
    const preset = findPreset(presetId);
    const statusEl = $('presetModeStatus');
    const detailEl = $('presetDetailContent');
    if (!statusEl || !detailEl) return;

    if (!preset) {
      statusEl.textContent = overriddenByUrl
        ? 'Custom Parameters (URL parameters overrode preset rules—calculating with explicit inputs)'
        : 'Custom Parameters (Supports any bank and airline ratio)';
      detailEl.innerHTML = 'If your issuer uses card-tier rules, limited-time campaign ratios, or quota limits (such as <strong>China Merchants Bank / CMB</strong> campaign-based transfers), check your bank\'s official app for the active campaign rate and enter "Every X bank points convert to Y airline miles" below. <strong style="color: #fde047;">Always verify the live transfer rules displayed in your rewards portal before transferring.</strong>';
      return;
    }

    const bonusVal = $('bonusPercent') ? parseFloat($('bonusPercent').value) : 0;
    const hasBonus = !isNaN(bonusVal) && bonusVal > 0;
    statusEl.textContent = hasBonus
      ? `Preset Applied: ${preset.labelEn} (with user-entered +${bonusVal}% promotional bonus assumption)`
      : `Preset Applied: ${preset.labelEn}`;

    const incBadge = preset.incrementVerified
      ? `${preset.increment.toLocaleString('en-US')} increment (Verified)`
      : `Pre-filled ${preset.increment.toLocaleString('en-US')} illustrative step assumption (Increment unverified in public terms, not an officially confirmed value)`;

    const partnerSourceHtml = (preset.partnerSourceUrl && preset.partnerSourceNameEn)
      ? ` | <a href="${preset.partnerSourceUrl}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: #7dd3fc; text-decoration: underline;">${preset.partnerSourceNameEn}</a>`
      : '';

    detailEl.innerHTML = `
      <div><strong>Issuing Region:</strong> ${preset.regionLabelEn} | <strong>Min &amp; Increment:</strong> ${preset.minTransfer.toLocaleString('en-US')} min transfer, ${incBadge}</div>
      <div style="margin-top:0.25rem;"><strong>Field Verification Status:</strong> ${preset.fieldStatusEn}</div>
      <div style="margin-top:0.25rem;"><strong>Card Eligibility:</strong> ${preset.eligibilityEn}</div>
      <div style="margin-top:0.25rem;"><strong>Promotional Bonus Note:</strong> Presets define base transfer parameters only; the Transfer Bonus field (currently ${hasBonus ? '+' + bonusVal + '%' : '0%'}) is a user-entered promotional assumption, not an inherent preset rule.</div>
      <div style="margin-top:0.25rem;"><strong>Official Sources:</strong> <a href="${preset.sourceUrl}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: #7dd3fc; text-decoration: underline;">${preset.sourceNameEn}</a>${partnerSourceHtml} (Last verified: ${preset.lastVerified})</div>
      <div style="margin-top:0.25rem; color:#fde047;"><strong>Reminder:</strong> Always verify the live transfer rules displayed in your rewards portal before transferring. Editing ratio, min transfer, or increment switches to Custom mode.</div>
    `;
  }

  function switchToCustomMode(keepTargetProgram = false) {
    if (isApplyingPreset) return;
    const sel = $('transferPreset');
    if (sel && sel.value !== 'custom') {
      sel.value = 'custom';
      if (!keepTargetProgram && $('targetProgram')) {
        $('targetProgram').value = '';
      }
      updatePresetMetaUI('custom');
    }
  }

  function applyPreset(presetId) {
    const preset = findPreset(presetId);
    if (!preset) {
      updatePresetMetaUI('custom');
      return;
    }
    isApplyingPreset = true;
    $('ratioPoints').value = preset.ratioPoints;
    $('ratioMiles').value = preset.ratioMiles;
    exactRatio = preset.ratioMiles / preset.ratioPoints;
    $('baseRatio').value = Number(exactRatio.toFixed(6));
    $('minTransfer').value = preset.minTransfer;
    $('increment').value = preset.increment;
    $('targetProgram').value = preset.targetProgramEn;
    minTransferManuallyEdited = true;
    updatePresetMetaUI(presetId);
    isApplyingPreset = false;
  }

  function syncFromHumanRatio() {
    switchToCustomMode();
    const rp = parseFloat($('ratioPoints').value);
    const rm = parseFloat($('ratioMiles').value);
    if (!isNaN(rp) && !isNaN(rm) && rp > 0 && rm > 0 && isFinite(rp) && isFinite(rm)) {
      exactRatio = rm / rp;
      $('baseRatio').value = Number(exactRatio.toFixed(6));
    } else {
      exactRatio = NaN;
      $('baseRatio').value = '';
    }
    calculateConversion();
  }

  function syncFromBaseRatio() {
    switchToCustomMode();
    const r = parseFloat($('baseRatio').value);
    if (!isNaN(r) && r > 0 && isFinite(r)) {
      exactRatio = r;
      $('ratioPoints').value = 1;
      $('ratioMiles').value = r;
    } else {
      exactRatio = r;
    }
    calculateConversion();
  }

  function initFromUrlParams() {
    const params = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search);
    const presetParam = params.get('preset');
    if (presetParam && findPreset(presetParam)) {
      $('transferPreset').value = presetParam;
      applyPreset(presetParam);
    }

    const parseNum = (key, maxVal = 1000000000) => {
      if (!params.has(key)) return null;
      const val = parseFloat(params.get(key));
      if (!isNaN(val) && isFinite(val) && val >= 0 && val <= maxVal) return val;
      return null;
    };

    const pts = parseNum('points') ?? parseNum('bankPoints');
    if (pts !== null) $('bankPoints').value = pts;

    const rp = parseNum('ratioPoints');
    const rm = parseNum('ratioMiles');
    const br = parseNum('baseRatio');

    if (rp !== null && rm !== null && rp > 0 && rm > 0) {
      if (br !== null && br > 0 && Math.abs((rm / rp) - br) > 1e-4) {
        $('baseRatio').value = br;
        exactRatio = br;
        $('ratioPoints').value = 1;
        $('ratioMiles').value = br;
      } else {
        $('ratioPoints').value = rp;
        $('ratioMiles').value = rm;
        exactRatio = rm / rp;
        $('baseRatio').value = Number(exactRatio.toFixed(6));
      }
    } else if (br !== null && br > 0) {
      $('baseRatio').value = br;
      exactRatio = br;
      $('ratioPoints').value = 1;
      $('ratioMiles').value = br;
    }

    const bonus = parseNum('bonusPercent');
    if (bonus !== null) $('bonusPercent').value = bonus;

    const inc = parseNum('increment');
    if (inc !== null && inc > 0) {
      $('increment').value = inc;
      if (!params.has('minTransfer') && !presetParam) {
        $('minTransfer').value = inc;
      }
    }

    const minT = parseNum('minTransfer');
    if (minT !== null && minT > 0) {
      $('minTransfer').value = minT;
      minTransferManuallyEdited = true;
    }

    if (params.has('targetProgram')) {
      $('targetProgram').value = params.get('targetProgram').slice(0, 60);
    }

    if (presetParam && findPreset(presetParam)) {
      const preset = findPreset(presetParam);
      const presetRatio = preset.ratioMiles / preset.ratioPoints;
      const currentMinT = parseFloat($('minTransfer').value);
      const currentInc = parseFloat($('increment').value);
      const ratioMatches = !isNaN(exactRatio) && Math.abs(exactRatio - presetRatio) <= 1e-6;
      const minTMatches = !isNaN(currentMinT) && currentMinT === preset.minTransfer;
      const incMatches = !isNaN(currentInc) && currentInc === preset.increment;
      const targetProgMatches = !params.has('targetProgram') ||
        params.get('targetProgram').trim() === preset.targetProgramEn;

      if (!ratioMatches || !minTMatches || !incMatches || !targetProgMatches) {
        $('transferPreset').value = 'custom';
        if (!params.has('targetProgram') && $('targetProgram')) {
          $('targetProgram').value = '';
        }
        updatePresetMetaUI('custom', true);
      } else {
        updatePresetMetaUI(presetParam);
      }
    }
  }

  function renderExplainSafe(transferablePoints, totalMiles, targetProg, remainingBankPoints) {
    const el = $('explain');
    if (!el) return;
    el.textContent = '';

    const appendStrong = (text) => {
      const s = document.createElement('strong');
      s.textContent = text;
      el.appendChild(s);
    };

    el.appendChild(document.createTextNode('You can transfer '));
    appendStrong(transferablePoints.toLocaleString('en-US'));
    el.appendChild(document.createTextNode(' points to receive '));
    appendStrong(totalMiles.toLocaleString('en-US', { maximumFractionDigits: 0 }));
    el.appendChild(document.createTextNode(` ${targetProg} miles.`));

    if (remainingBankPoints > 0) {
      el.appendChild(document.createTextNode(' You will have '));
      appendStrong(remainingBankPoints.toLocaleString('en-US'));
      el.appendChild(document.createTextNode(' points left in your bank account due to increment restrictions.'));
    }
  }

  function calculateConversion() {
    let points = parseFloat($('bankPoints').value);
    let ratio = (!isNaN(exactRatio) && exactRatio > 0) ? exactRatio : parseFloat($('baseRatio').value);
    let bonus = parseFloat($('bonusPercent').value);
    let inc = parseFloat($('increment').value);
    let minTransferEl = $('minTransfer');
    let minTransfer = minTransferEl ? parseFloat(minTransferEl.value) : NaN;
    let targetProg = $('targetProgram').value.trim() || 'airline';

    const resetState = (msg = 'Please enter valid numbers.') => {
      $('totalMiles').textContent = '-';
      $('explain').textContent = msg;
      $('transferablePoints').textContent = '-';
      $('remainingPoints').textContent = '-';
      $('baseMiles').textContent = '-';
      $('bonusMiles').textContent = '-';
      $('effectiveRatio').textContent = '-';
    };

    if (isNaN(points) || isNaN(ratio) || isNaN(bonus) || isNaN(inc) || isNaN(minTransfer)) {
      resetState('Please enter valid numbers (points, ratio, minimum transfer, and increment cannot be empty).');
      return;
    }

    if (!isFinite(points) || !isFinite(ratio) || !isFinite(bonus) || !isFinite(inc) || !isFinite(minTransfer)) {
      resetState('Inputs are too large.');
      return;
    }

    if (points < 0 || ratio <= 0 || bonus < 0 || inc <= 0 || minTransfer <= 0) {
      resetState('Inputs cannot be negative. Ratio, minimum transfer, and increment must be greater than 0.');
      return;
    }

    if (points === 0) {
      resetState('Enter your bank points to see how many miles you will receive.');
      return;
    }

    let transferablePoints = Math.floor(points / inc) * inc;
    let remainingBankPoints = points - transferablePoints;
    const minValidTransfer = Math.ceil(minTransfer / inc) * inc;

    if (points < minTransfer || transferablePoints === 0 || transferablePoints < minTransfer) {
      resetState(`You need at least ${minValidTransfer} points to make a transfer: under the ${inc} increment rule, your transferable amount (${transferablePoints} points) is below the ${minTransfer} minimum transfer threshold (total transferred must be a multiple of ${inc} and at least ${minTransfer}).`);
      return;
    }

    let baseMiles = Math.round(transferablePoints * ratio * 1e6) / 1e6;
    let bonusMiles = Math.round(baseMiles * (bonus / 100) * 1e6) / 1e6;
    let totalMiles = Math.round((baseMiles + bonusMiles) * 1e6) / 1e6;
    let effectiveRatio = totalMiles / transferablePoints;

    $('totalMiles').textContent = totalMiles.toLocaleString('en-US', {maximumFractionDigits:0}) + ' Miles';
    renderExplainSafe(transferablePoints, totalMiles, targetProg, remainingBankPoints);

    $('transferablePoints').textContent = transferablePoints.toLocaleString('en-US');
    $('remainingPoints').textContent = remainingBankPoints.toLocaleString('en-US');
    $('baseMiles').textContent = baseMiles.toLocaleString('en-US', {maximumFractionDigits:0});
    $('bonusMiles').textContent = bonusMiles.toLocaleString('en-US', {maximumFractionDigits:0});
    $('effectiveRatio').textContent = effectiveRatio.toLocaleString('en-US', {maximumFractionDigits:4});
  }

  if ($('transferPreset')) {
    $('transferPreset').addEventListener('change', (e) => {
      const val = e.target.value;
      if (val === 'custom') {
        updatePresetMetaUI('custom');
      } else {
        applyPreset(val);
      }
      calculateConversion();
    });
  }

  if ($('ratioPoints')) $('ratioPoints').addEventListener('input', syncFromHumanRatio);
  if ($('ratioMiles')) $('ratioMiles').addEventListener('input', syncFromHumanRatio);
  if ($('baseRatio')) $('baseRatio').addEventListener('input', syncFromBaseRatio);

  if ($('increment')) {
    $('increment').addEventListener('input', () => {
      switchToCustomMode();
      const incVal = parseFloat($('increment').value);
      if (!minTransferManuallyEdited && $('minTransfer') && !isNaN(incVal) && incVal > 0) {
        $('minTransfer').value = $('increment').value;
      }
      calculateConversion();
    });
  }

  if ($('minTransfer')) {
    $('minTransfer').addEventListener('input', () => {
      minTransferManuallyEdited = true;
      switchToCustomMode();
      calculateConversion();
    });
  }

  ['bankPoints', 'bonusPercent', 'targetProgram'].forEach(id => {
    if ($(id)) {
      $(id).addEventListener('input', () => {
        if (id === 'targetProgram') {
          switchToCustomMode(true);
        } else if (id === 'bonusPercent' && $('transferPreset') && $('transferPreset').value !== 'custom') {
          updatePresetMetaUI($('transferPreset').value);
        }
        calculateConversion();
      });
    }
  });

  if ($('btnShare')) {
    $('btnShare').addEventListener('click', () => {
      const url = new URL(window.location.origin + window.location.pathname);
      const points = parseFloat($('bankPoints').value);
      const rp = parseFloat($('ratioPoints').value);
      const rm = parseFloat($('ratioMiles').value);
      const ratio = parseFloat($('baseRatio').value);
      const bonus = parseFloat($('bonusPercent').value);
      const inc = parseFloat($('increment').value);
      const minT = parseFloat($('minTransfer').value);
      const presetVal = $('transferPreset') ? $('transferPreset').value : 'custom';

      if (presetVal && presetVal !== 'custom') url.searchParams.set('preset', presetVal);
      if (points > 0) url.searchParams.set('points', points);
      if (rp > 0) url.searchParams.set('ratioPoints', rp);
      if (rm > 0) url.searchParams.set('ratioMiles', rm);
      if (ratio > 0) url.searchParams.set('baseRatio', ratio);
      if (bonus >= 0) url.searchParams.set('bonusPercent', bonus);
      if (inc > 0) url.searchParams.set('increment', inc);
      if (minT > 0) url.searchParams.set('minTransfer', minT);

      navigator.clipboard.writeText(url.toString()).then(() => {
        const toast = $('toast');
        if (toast) {
          toast.classList.add('show');
          setTimeout(() => toast.classList.remove('show'), 2000);
        }
      });
    });
  }

  initFromUrlParams();
  calculateConversion();
</script>
